spec:
  grid: 30x30, single background color (any of 0-9)
  corners:
    count: 2-3 of the 4 grid corners hold a unique marker color pixel
    distribution: TL and TR most common; at most 1 bottom corner used [observed]
    corner_5x5_region: entirely background except the single corner pixel in input
  sprites:
    count: 4-5 total, each with a unique body color
    size: 5x5 bounding box; body occupies 4-15 pixels, marker occupies exactly 1 pixel, rest is background
    connectivity: may be disconnected (even 8-conn); no structural constraint
    grouping: each sprite belongs to exactly one marker group (1-3 sprites per marker)
    placement: no two sprites overlap; no sprite overlaps any corner 5x5 region; min gap >=1 cell
    body_color: globally unique - appears only within its 5x5 window
    marker_pixel: exactly 1 pixel of a marker color embedded in the sprite
  colors: 7-9 distinct (1 bg + 2-3 markers + 4-5 body colors); all 10 ARC colors available
  transform:
    per_sprite: recolor body pixels to marker color; recolor marker pixel to body color (exception below)
    side_collision: if marker pixel is on the column facing its corner (col 0 for left corners, col 4 for right) AND another same-group sprite has body at that local cell, use that other body color instead
    corner_composite: paint the union of all same-marker sprite masks (full 5x5 foreground) into the corner 5x5 region using the marker color; hidden vertical tails (single-owner columns not reaching target edge, flanked by other owners) are omitted

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose bg color and pick 2-3 corners; assign each a unique marker color.
    2. Decide sprite count (4-5) and distribute among markers (1-3 each).
    3. For each marker group, design 5x5 sprite masks (random patterns, 4-15 foreground pixels each, exactly 1 designated marker-pixel position). Ensure the union composite for the corner is non-trivial.
    4. Assign unique body colors to sprites; place each sprite at a random non-overlapping position on the 30x30 grid (avoiding corner 5x5 zones and other sprites).
    5. Fill each sprite window: body color for body pixels, marker color for the single marker pixel, bg elsewhere. Set the single corner pixel.
    6. Verify solver produces correct output (validates all constraints including hidden-tail logic).
